# The capstone as it was written before M-VEC: every vectorization spelled out.
# examples/capstone.golfj now says all four of these with bare + and *, and
# prints exactly the same four lines.  This file exists so the explicit forms
# stay compiled and output-checked forever — ⊞ zip-with a ′atom quotation, and
# broadcast built by hand out of a named variable, a closure word and ′f€.
# Nothing here is deprecated: € ⇤ ⌿ ⊞ are how a list meets a function that is
# not one of the five polymorphic operators, which is most functions.
# DO NOT shorten this file.  Not shrinking is its entire job.
